{"title":"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(manipulation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (manipulation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_Clear\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 Clear</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_(Pythagorean_Theorem_&amp;_Square_of_Binomial)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 (Pythagorean Theorem &amp; Square of Binomial)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Daniel finds a rectangular index card and measures its diagonal to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> centimeters.\nDaniel then cuts out equal squares of side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm at two opposite corners of the index card and measures the distance between the two closest vertices of these squares to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f3f43ae8f8f1306b3547283e641e1df970167ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> centimeters, as shown below. What is the area of the original index card?\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/f/22f9f7a96f6ad58ba5a6b8396b925cd53152cf24.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] // Diagram by MRENTHUSIASM, edited by Djmathman size(200); defaultpen(linewidth(0.6)); draw((489.5,-213) -- (225.5,-213) -- (225.5,-185) -- (199.5,-185) -- (198.5,-62) -- (457.5,-62) -- (457.5,-93) -- (489.5,-93) -- cycle); draw((206.29,-70.89) -- (480.21,-207.11), linetype (&quot;6 6&quot;),Arrows(size=4,arrowhead=HookHead)); draw((237.85,-182.24) -- (448.65,-95.76),linetype (&quot;6 6&quot;),Arrows(size=4,arrowhead=HookHead)); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(450,-80)); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(475,-106)); label(&quot;$8$&quot;,(300,-103)); label(&quot;$4\\sqrt 2$&quot;,(300,-173)); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"175\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/6/4566176ba0e46f2e90feb75d0ed914ca95785bff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 14 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 10\\sqrt{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 16 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 12\\sqrt{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"449\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/c/46c58f38312c56694cd1890f9c251f64ec6f7dd2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Edited by MRENTHUSIASM */ size(250); real x, y; x = 6; y = 3; draw((0,0)--(x,0)); draw((0,0)--(0,y)); draw((0,y)--(x,y)); draw((x,0)--(x,y)); draw((0.5,0)--(0.5,0.5)--(0,0.5)); draw((x-0.5,y)--(x-0.5,y-0.5)--(x,y-0.5)); draw((0.5,0.5)--(x-0.5,y-0.5),dashed,Arrows()); draw((x,0)--(0,y),dashed,Arrows()); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(x-0.5,y-0.25),W); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(x-0.25,y-0.5),S); label(&quot;$8$&quot;,midpoint((0.5,y-0.5)--(x/2,y/2)),(0,2.5)); label(&quot;$4\\sqrt{2}$&quot;,midpoint((0.5,0.5)--(x/2,y/2)),S); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(0,0),SW); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,(0,0.5),W); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,(0.5,0),S); label(&quot;$I$&quot;,(0.5,0.5),N); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,(x,y),NE); label(&quot;$G$&quot;,(x-0.5,y),N); label(&quot;$H$&quot;,(x,y-0.5),E); label(&quot;$J$&quot;,(x-0.5,y-0.5),S); Label L1 = Label(&quot;$w$&quot;, align=(0,0), position=MidPoint, filltype=Fill(3,0,white)); Label L2 = Label(&quot;$\\ell$&quot;, align=(0,0), position=MidPoint, filltype=Fill(0,3,white)); draw((0,-1)--(x,-1), L=L1, arrow=Arrows(),bar=Bars(15)); draw((x+1,0)--(x+1,y), L=L2, arrow=Arrows(),bar=Bars(15)); [/asy]\" width=\"418\" height=\"255\" />\nLabel the bottom left corner of the larger rectangle (without the square cut out) as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and the top right as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> is the width of the rectangle and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> is the length. Now we have vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/e/3aeae5cdffa852d1d28cb919190626dc0a28baf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E, F, G, H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" /> as vertices of the irregular octagon created by cutting out the squares. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e12c1106a2c6daceb6f79385d99639c096adca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I, J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> be the two closest vertices formed by the squares.\nThe distance between the two closest vertices of the squares is thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/9/b394779e4a6f009f46ad5e69095fbb36c5cbe1ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IJ=\\left(4\\sqrt{2}\\right).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"110\" height=\"34\" />\nSubstituting, we get: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/3/ae31eb53986921a8e5b41f6caa23b2f3797d15ff.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(IJ)^2 = (w-2)^2 + (\\ell-2)^2 = \\left(4\\sqrt{2}\\right)^2 = 32 \\implies w^2+\\ell^2-4w-4\\ell = 24.\\]\" width=\"536\" height=\"35\" />\nUsing the fact that the diagonal of the rectangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/a/12a9fb4c5b23667e57f28d844ad99715f18ba3fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> we get: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/e/48e7b02cdfb36277be0b58a3c913b8018e90ad5b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[w^2+\\ell^2 = 64.\\]\" width=\"103\" height=\"17\" />\nSubtracting the first equation from the second equation, we get: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/b/a3bf4cdf8bfc438cd8f50589b76aa8b4ab67d736.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4w+4\\ell=40 \\implies w+\\ell = 10.\\]\" width=\"242\" height=\"14\" />\nSquaring yields: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/4/96447fbf7ed654c45257ac25f40fda25ca5a46f3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[w^2 + 2w\\ell + \\ell^2 = 100.\\]\" width=\"164\" height=\"17\" />\nSubtracting the second equation from this, we get: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/2/192eb0f3d545f2acce2a32eb5d183108411b78e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2w\\ell = 36,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> and thus the area of the original rectangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027c63fc083958e19222f338a60374545db9e028.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w\\ell = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 18}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"115\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~USAMO333\n</p><p>Edits and Diagram by ~KingRavi and ~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p><p>Minor edit by yanes04\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/SRV4e74qsM8\">https://youtu.be/SRV4e74qsM8</a>\n</p><p>Let x be the width of the original rectangle and y be the height. Through observation and logic, we can then conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/a/42a711118e3a45d8df8d7faa620d097cc8dcb246.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x-2)^2 + (y-2)^2 = 32.\\]\" width=\"192\" height=\"20\" /> After expanding and simplifying the expressions, you end up with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/a/72aeb27d43a68ab1a25f2595a4450ab1c79274f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y=10.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"17\" /> If you then solve for x in terms of y, you end up with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/d/8bdfbb82c54ae9b1af6310c076576e14bd7abbec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=10-y.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"17\" /> Since 8 is the diagonal of the original rectangle, we can write that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/d/86d99d8a4621678c2f89c4f50b028751f10322ae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(10-y)^2+y^2=64.\\]\" width=\"155\" height=\"20\" /> Use the quadratic formula to solve for y, and then solve for x. Using either root, yields a product of the difference of squares, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/0/54021f410337ebb2f974649f7bf61c05bdd99573.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25-7=18.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"99\" height=\"15\" /> Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/5/0a556c278db249c883fb693287adb75766e820f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" /> is our solution!\n</p><p>~Namya\n</p><p>Note: I just changed it into Latex as it looked a little bit unclear.\n</p><p>~moonwatcher0201\n</p><p>Note: This is incredibly similar to Solution 1. In fact, the only difference is the method of Algebra used to calculate the final answer, which in my opinion doesn’t really constitute a whole new solution.\n</p><p>~ilee0820\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28manipulation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(manipulation)\">Solution 3 (manipulation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (manipulation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the variable names be as in Solution 1. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/4/ae4aafe7d60b883baa13ab3021447d15a78e1526.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l^2+w^2=64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" /> (I) and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/f/c6f780283d3d88b1f3c744052b040b0dedb11226.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(l-2)^2+(w-2)^2=32\\implies l^2+w^2-4l-4w+4+4=32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"484\" height=\"21\" /> (II). Substituting the LHS of (I) into (II) and simplifying, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/9/a093dcc38949e0fc4d4eb3c45d116f7bfbdc8330.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64-4(l+w)=24\\implies l+w=16-6=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"357\" height=\"20\" /> (III). Let (IV) be (III)<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/b/daba4d2c72c882485efe31ce15640ac17cb05336.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^2-$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"18\" />(I). Then, (IV) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/2/0c2c4701444dbe3f879639320075d642b19ed8bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2lw=36 \\implies lw = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"184\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/5/0a556c278db249c883fb693287adb75766e820f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" /> is our solution!\n</p><p>~GoldemGem4848\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/BIy0Koe4D4s\">https://youtu.be/BIy0Koe4D4s</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_Clear\">Video Solution 1 Clear</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 Clear\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rDE8Yyx20ZI\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rDE8Yyx20ZI</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_2_.28Pythagorean_Theorem_.26_Square_of_Binomial.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_(Pythagorean_Theorem_&amp;_Square_of_Binomial)\">Video Solution 2 (Pythagorean Theorem &amp; Square of Binomial)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 (Pythagorean Theorem &amp; Square of Binomial)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rJ61GqU6NWM&amp;list=PLmpPPbOoDfgj5BlPtEAGcB7BR_UA5FgFj&amp;index=5\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rJ61GqU6NWM&amp;list=PLmpPPbOoDfgj5BlPtEAGcB7BR_UA5FgFj&amp;index=5</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A\">2022 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10